Have you ever heard of Boxing Day?

6
00:00:21,080 --> 00:00:28,000
The celebration happens in the United Kingdom and the countries that were once part

7
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:29,290
of the British Empire.

8
00:00:30,600 --> 00:00:34,420
Boxing Day falls on the day after Christmas.

9
00:00:35,500 --> 00:00:44,440
The official holiday dates back to 1871, yet no one is exactly sure how it started.

10
00:00:44,440 --> 00:00:50,420
Some people think it has something to do with Christmas gifts.

11
00:00:51,700 --> 00:00:55,380
In Britain, on the 26th of December,

12
00:00:56,060 --> 00:00:57,800
the day after Christmas,

13
00:00:58,480 --> 00:01:05,540
the very rich people in Victorian times gave gifts to their servants in small boxes.

14
00:01:05,540 --> 00:01:09,760
That's why it was called Boxing Day.

15
00:01:11,100 --> 00:01:17,120
Another possibility is that the name refers to money that was given to people in

16
00:01:17,120 --> 00:01:23,780
need. Traditionally, a box was placed in churches to collect money.

17
00:01:24,800 --> 00:01:30,780
The money from the box was given out to the poor on the day after Christmas.

18
00:01:30,780 --> 00:01:38,900
No matter what Boxing Day's origins are, it's still a widely celebrated holiday.

19
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:48,300
For some, it is a big shopping day, and for others, it is a great day to eat, relax,

20
